To distinguish the wand of death apart from the wand of sleep
*immediately* is what I find the worst part in your proposal
(aside from valid the sacr-fodder argument to consider).

Would you really find it hard to recognize whether a bug is
slow or fast? Well, maybe; then it would become a bit more
difficult to get intrinsic permanent speed as uncomplicated
as it is now with the wand.

For me the bug proposal would be a nice gimmick feature, but
it's a "meta-pun"; without the existing message system and
the actual messages no one would think about generating bug
monsters when engraving with the three types of wands. I am
very unsure whether it's worth to implement the proposed new
monster generation pop-up mechanism for that purpose.

